{"title":"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Area_Ratio_Between_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Area Ratio Between Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is 8 square inches. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are midpoints of congruent segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/95915f5885ed19f737ac8338c7c0b1d0e23fb73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XY}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba3704899aa86f3eace66b2bbe084b78320cb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XZ}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aae5af60fe3607abf94eb267d4f1b9f28138c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XC}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1817c383636a4e8f30eb3ebb5c8a26dd172742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{YZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. The area (in square inches) of the shaded region is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a879a53da609c8f6948eef78732e18f14a90fe4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* AMC8 2002 #20 Problem */ draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(5,4)--cycle); draw((2.5,2)--(7.5,2)); draw((5,4)--(5,0)); fill((0,0)--(2.5,2)--(5,2)--(5,0)--cycle, mediumgrey); label(scale(0.8)*&quot;$X$&quot;, (5,4), N); label(scale(0.8)*&quot;$Y$&quot;, (0,0), W); label(scale(0.8)*&quot;$Z$&quot;, (10,0), E); label(scale(0.8)*&quot;$A$&quot;, (2.5,2.2), W); label(scale(0.8)*&quot;$B$&quot;, (7.5,2.2), E); label(scale(0.8)*&quot;$C$&quot;, (5,0), S); fill((0,-.8)--(1,-.8)--(1,-.95)--cycle, white);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19bbf9e1f91e5e040c5ef6d08682761cea589bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\frac{1}2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\frac{1}2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3\\frac{1}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"387\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square inches. The area of a triangle can also be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ce4b902246a68e80a0f0417d8072f96cde6fb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{bh}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"39\" /> or in this problem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/8/da85dc8ae227b81b375f891de06550be8e93b908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XC\\cdot YZ}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />. By solving, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e08e6d320f1c6830cef20de6bbf4399b5722e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{XC\\cdot YZ}{2} = 8,\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/84667c66408f8ed434a0d7fefd303a5b81f24cbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XC\\cdot YZ = 16.\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"12\" /> \n</p><p>With SAS congruence, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6de842d3349af1c711b693327a83ef2513085ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XCY$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4d9640fa7ee3fc5ca6d840b51a746a78ec10fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XCZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are congruent. Hence, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/24891d483ca2ee9c5cf948c859533d915070bcb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XCY = \\frac{8}{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"116\" height=\"37\" />. (Let's say point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection between line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4c77c87b3275e481b1d07085e15fd2f0788dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.) We can find the area of the trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bdac043eb28a96901d341a58db13c3d0e3ef18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADCY$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> by subtracting the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d63e215df82aa91e3858ff3384dc7326222a509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XAD$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We find the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d63e215df82aa91e3858ff3384dc7326222a509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XAD$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ce4b902246a68e80a0f0417d8072f96cde6fb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{bh}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"39\" /> formula- <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd930dd9672fc4cc621e0f012fa51e7a9335b8d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XD\\cdot AD}{2} = \\frac{\\frac{XC}{2}\\cdot AD}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"40\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> from solution 1. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d63e215df82aa91e3858ff3384dc7326222a509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XAD$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3effd38d41efdd1f62bcc3171bfcec110527db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{XC}{2}\\cdot \\frac{YZ}{4}}{2} = \\frac{16}{16} = 1\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the area of the shaded area- trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bdac043eb28a96901d341a58db13c3d0e3ef18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADCY$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edcfff8478f915989dd575173252014977042ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-1 = \\boxed{\\text{(D)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"116\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n- sarah07\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can guess that Triangle XAB has an area of 1/4 of XYZ, so 2, and polygon ABZY has 6, so the shaded area would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/90348d6f185fb89af01e8c1cc6f24aa1e912b601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"52\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we call point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> the point of intersection between segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4c77c87b3275e481b1d07085e15fd2f0788dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we can split trapezoids <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bdac043eb28a96901d341a58db13c3d0e3ef18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADCY$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2ecb1093b21b9a745cf6769e8be2e209c7580e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDCY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> into triangles and rectangles.\n</p><p>These new triangles are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f332ac9219e1017d0538e481fad4e4788bc658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c5447d6e1867e713c83dca86f071256e78d96c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XDB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, and the rectangles are double the area of any of these triangles. \n</p><p>So, the total area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3039f01ba9e41f5490b7130e344be554015a25b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XYZ$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bbfe131e3a05d3e7e32f637be76c9aa727b733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\cdot [\\triangle AXD]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>That means the area of the bottom-left triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/1507ff38275381406bbe3f811a6d61787b3bdf66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{8}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />. The rectangle next to it is double that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>In total, the area of shaded trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bdac043eb28a96901d341a58db13c3d0e3ef18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADCY$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/90348d6f185fb89af01e8c1cc6f24aa1e912b601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"52\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n- AidenJ73\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Area_Ratio_Between_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Area_Ratio_Between_Triangles)\">Video Solution (Area Ratio Between Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Area Ratio Between Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zwy5U5IQi88\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zwy5U5IQi88</a>  ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wIVHVxhA7xg\">https://youtu.be/wIVHVxhA7xg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 8\">2002 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1